@page "/docs/components/toc"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.TableOfContents
<PageTitle>Table of Contents - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Table of Contents</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="toc" />
        </div>
        <p>An "On This Page" nav that lists a region's headings and highlights the one you're reading. It scans for headings (assigning ids where missing), follows scrolling, and scrolls smoothly to a section on click. The right rail of this very site is one.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(TableOfContentsUsageExample)"
                Description="Point ContentSelector at the region to scan and RootSelector at its scroll container; the nav lists the headings and tracks the one in view." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default"
          Description="Set RootSelector to a scrollable box and the nav tracks that box. Scroll the article - the active heading follows; click a link to jump."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Variants"
          Description="List is the plain set of links. Rail draws a hairline down the start edge with one indicator that slides between sections. Progress adds a fill that follows how far the region has scrolled. Marks is a minimap of dashes, sized by heading level, that reveals all its labels on hover or keyboard focus - and Peek is that minimap with the panel taken away, opening one label at a time (its own demos are below)."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsVariantsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Marks, floating"
          Description="The minimap on its own, pinned to the start edge and centred. Hover it (or Tab into it) and the labels slide out, staggered down the list. Passing absolute in Class scopes it to this box instead of the viewport."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsMarksExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Peek, wave"
          Description="Wave gives Peek's column a dock-style magnification: the line under the pointer grows the longest, its neighbours a step less, the next pair less still, and the swell follows the cursor smoothly down the column. Tabbing through the links plays the same wave, and each line still peeks its own label. The column packs tighter than plain Peek so the swell has room to read. Because a tick's length reads its heading level, sections that all sit at one level - a step list, a timeline, a changelog - draw an even column of equal lines, which is what the swell reads cleanest against. PeekContent carries what the ticks drop: here each card names the step, says what it does and adds a line of metadata. Two knobs retune the geometry: MarkWidth sets the resting length of a section line (every level derives from it, on any minimap variant), WaveAmplitude how far the hovered line grows."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsWaveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Peek"
          Description="The minimap with no panel and no title: just ticks, and hovering one (or tabbing to it) opens that heading's card alone. Tick length reads the heading level - long for h2, shorter for what nests under it - so the column sketches the shape of the page. PeekContent replaces the card's body, here a heading plus a line of description. The card opens away from the edge the panel is pinned to."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsPeekExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Position"
          Description="Six anchors: start or end, top, centre or bottom. The edges are logical, so a Start panel sits on the left in LTR and on the right in RTL, and each one slides in from the edge it belongs to. Inline (the default) leaves the panel in the layout flow. The panel floats bare - see Customization for the classes that turn it into a card."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsPositionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Top-level only"
          Description="Narrow HeadingSelector to skip sub-headings, and set your own title."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsFlatExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="LinkClass restyles every link (merged over the defaults, so data-active: variants win) - here an accent bar and tint mark the active section. Pair it with a custom icon title, Sticky to pin the panel, and Class to set the width. The panel carries no surface of its own, floating or inline, so the card here is Class too: bg-popover text-popover-foreground rounded-lg border p-3 shadow-md."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL"
          Description="Wrapped in a DirectionProvider with Arabic or Hebrew copy - the rail, list and active marker mirror to the right."
          Example="typeof(TableOfContentsRtlExample)" />
</div>

